  "summary": "If Everyone Knew is a free offline web page that teaches the handful of bystander skills most likely to save lives: hands-only CPR, choking, stroke recognition, severe bleeding, heart attack, the recovery position and how to help someone in suicidal crisis. Each skill comes with practice drills, such as a CPR metronome, branching scenarios and a ten-question test, plus a printable cheat sheet and a region picker that swaps in local emergency numbers."
